WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.340
And I don’t know if you guys know the story of Mossville where it was called Shoat's Prairie because of all the pigs . . . the hogs that they had.

2
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:17.820
And then . . . And I always told them whenever I would talk about Mossville, I would tell them that I was from Mossville proper.

3
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.000
The railroad track . . . There used to be a sign that said “Mossville.”

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.180
Anything from that railroad track right there all the way back down to . . . past the LaTours' was considered Mossville.

5
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:33.680
They built the school outside of the Mossville area because that was the largest piece of land that they had.

6
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.820
And of course then they built the Bel Air and Lincoln Heights subdivisions around it.

7
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.120
But that was the . . . This is the original Mossville.

8
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.600
Then when you went to Evergreen Road going north, which was called Saprack.

9
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.500
And the Braxtons, the LaDouxs, the Rigmaidens, they were all up there.

10
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:56.640
And down on my end was the Mosses . . . well on my . . . on the Perkins end was the Mosses and the Perkins.

11
00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.760
Got you.

12
00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.380
And it was called Perkinstown.

13
00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:10.060
So before it was Mossville, it was Perkinstown, which I’m from that end, and Saprack, which was the north . . . north end.

14
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.260
So do you know why your family came to Mossville?

15
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.580
From the history that we have for the Perkins and the Mosses, they were already here.

16
00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:32.020
They were in the . . . something they called Little Woods or Big Woods which was . . . As close as I can come to the actual location was in the Edgerly area,

17
00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:35.000
Vinton, over . . . Sulphur, in that area.

18
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.240
They were on a farm there.

19
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:48.160
And then they had the Homestead Act of 1862, and they came . . . Why they chose this area, I have no history of that.

20
00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:58.020
But I do know that my great great grandmother, Minerva Moss Perkins, homesteaded a hundred and sixty-two acres.

21
00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:02.080
That’s how the Perkins came here, and the Mosses did the same thing.

22
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.040
And the . . . She was a Moss, and married a Perkins.

23
00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.700
So both of those families were connected.

24
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:17.840
And then Griffin Braxton, he homesteaded a hundred and sixty-two acres up on Evergreen Road.
